\ A non-recursive word that fails AOT codegen with NC.13 (abstract stack
\ underflow). It declares one input but drops twice, so the second `drop` runs
\ against an empty abstract stack. The `--trace-aot=instr` per-instruction trace
\ fires for this non-recursive word and names the underflowing `drop` at sp=0,
\ the instruction the NC.13 rejection then reports. The old ONEZ_DEBUG_TRACE hook
\ printed nothing here because it fired only for self-tail-recursive words.
bad-nonrec: ( x -- ) [ drop drop ] ;
5 bad-nonrec
